==============================================================================
S1  Well-typing of the literal block layout
==============================================================================
Literal layout: block rows (A | 0 | 1 | 0), (0 | B | 0 | 1), (K_{m,n} | 0 | 0 | 1), (0 | K_{n,m} | 0 | 0)
Block row heights: m (A), n (B), m (K_{m,n} is m x n), n (K_{n,m} is n x m)  -> rows = 2m + 2n
Block column widths: m (A above K_{m,n}), n (B above K_{n,m}), 1, 1          -> cols = m + n + 2
Column 1 carries A (width m) and K_{m,n} (width n): consistent only if n = m.
Column 2 carries B (width n) and K_{n,m} (width m): consistent only if m = n.
Square iff 2m+2n = m+n+2 iff m+n = 2 iff m = n = 1.
  m=1 n=1 : rows=4 cols=4 square=True col-widths-consistent=True
  m=1 n=2 : rows=6 cols=5 square=False col-widths-consistent=False
  m=1 n=3 : rows=8 cols=6 square=False col-widths-consistent=False
  m=1 n=4 : rows=10 cols=7 square=False col-widths-consistent=False
  m=2 n=1 : rows=6 cols=5 square=False col-widths-consistent=False
  m=2 n=2 : rows=8 cols=6 square=False col-widths-consistent=True
  m=2 n=3 : rows=10 cols=7 square=False col-widths-consistent=False
  m=2 n=4 : rows=12 cols=8 square=False col-widths-consistent=False
  m=3 n=1 : rows=8 cols=6 square=False col-widths-consistent=False
  m=3 n=2 : rows=10 cols=7 square=False col-widths-consistent=False
  m=3 n=3 : rows=12 cols=8 square=False col-widths-consistent=True
  m=3 n=4 : rows=14 cols=9 square=False col-widths-consistent=False
  m=4 n=1 : rows=10 cols=7 square=False col-widths-consistent=False
  m=4 n=2 : rows=12 cols=8 square=False col-widths-consistent=False
  m=4 n=3 : rows=14 cols=9 square=False col-widths-consistent=False
  m=4 n=4 : rows=16 cols=10 square=False col-widths-consistent=True
Only square literal instance: m=n=1 with A=B=[0] (the 1-vertex tournament), K=[k], K'=[k'] with k,k' in {0,1}:
  k=0 k'=0 : charpoly = x**4 ; eigenvalues = {0: 4} ; max real eigenvalue = 0
  k=0 k'=1 : charpoly = x**2*(x - 1)*(x + 1) ; eigenvalues = {-1: 1, 1: 1, 0: 2} ; max real eigenvalue = 1
  k=1 k'=0 : charpoly = x**2*(x - 1)*(x + 1) ; eigenvalues = {-1: 1, 1: 1, 0: 2} ; max real eigenvalue = 1
  k=1 k'=1 : charpoly = (x - 1)**2*(x + 1)**2 ; eigenvalues = {1: 2, -1: 2} ; max real eigenvalue = 1

==============================================================================
S2  Consistent (m+n+2)-vertex reading and the exhaustive sweep
==============================================================================
Vertex order (V_A, V_B, alpha, beta).  M = [[A, K, 0, 0], [K', B, 0, 1_n], [1_m^T, 0, 0, 0], [0, 0, 0, 0]].
alpha = source (arcs alpha -> every vertex of V_A, no in-arcs); beta = sink (arcs every vertex of V_B -> beta, no out-arcs).
Cross-link orientations: ONE = K = J_{m,n}, K' = 0 ; TWO = K = J, K' = J^T (K + K^T both ways) ; ORI = K_ij = [i+j even], K' = J^T - K^T (an oriented bipartite cross-link, union is a tournament on m+n).
tournament iso classes on 1 vertices: 1
tournament iso classes on 2 vertices: 1
tournament iso classes on 3 vertices: 2
tournament iso classes on 4 vertices: 4

Sweep statistics (64 tournament pairs per orientation, matrices of size m+n+2 <= 10):
| orientation | total | all_zero | zero_mult_ge2 | has_nonzero_pure_imag | has_negative_real_eig | all_re_negative | max_re_ge0 | perron_positive | block_triangular_factor_ok |
| ONE | 64 | 16 | 64 | 0 | 48 | 0 | 64 | 48 | 64 |
| TWO | 64 | 0 | 64 | 0 | 64 | 0 | 64 | 64 | 0 |
| ORI | 64 | 2 | 64 | 0 | 62 | 0 | 64 | 62 | 2 |

